  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Slice chicken breasts into very thin pieces (freeze slightly if desired to make this easier) and place in a medium bowl.  Add next 4 ingredients (worcestershire through ground pepper) and stir to coat chicken.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat 1 teaspoon olive oil in a large (9\") oven proof skillet.  Add chicken pieces and cook until browned -about 5 minutes. Turn pieces over and cook about 2-3 minutes more or until brown.  Remove from skillet.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Add remaining 1 teaspoon olive oil to warm skillet. Then add onions, bell pepper and garlic.  Cook and stir to heated and tender- 2-3 minutes.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Turn heat off and add chicken back to skillet and stir with veggies to combine.  Place sliced cheese over all and cover 2-3 minutes to melt.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Note: Serve up in bowls for those eating low carb.  Serve with warm hoagie rolls for others.",
      "group": null
    }
  ],
